The Lorentz transformation in units with $c=1$ is $\begin{aligned}
x'&=\frac{x-vt}{\sqrt{1-v^2}},\\
t'&=\frac{t-vx}{\sqrt{1-v^2}}.
\end{aligned}$ Its inverse is $\begin{aligned}
x&=\frac{x'+vt'}{\sqrt{1-v^2}},\\
t&=\frac{t'+vx'}{\sqrt{1-v^2}}.\end{aligned}$

